Font family names referenced without bundling a font
----------------------------------------------------

Five product-pack families (`cinematic-fog-title`, `cinematic-rain-launch`,
`editorial-liquid-surface`, `keyed-subject-promo`, `tracked-callout-overlay`)
and several fixture packages name only the CSS generic `sans-serif` or
`monospace`, which the renderer resolves against whatever the host installs. Two
fixture packages (`fixtures/packages/lower-third`,
`fixtures/packages/keyframed-lower-third`) and two non-package fixture documents
(`fixtures/canvas/frame-selection.json`, `fixtures/cut/import-plan.expected.json`)
still name `Inter` without shipping a font file; they are render/import test
inputs, not distributed template content. Naming a font family is not
redistribution of Font Software and creates no OFL obligation. The font files
this repository actually distributes are exactly the WOFF2 files recorded above.


Runtime dependency boundary
---------------------------

ShellX Motion does not vendor any third-party source code, and no `node_modules`
content is tracked in this repository. Runtime components stay outside the tree:

  - `playwright-core` (Apache-2.0) is a declared npm dependency of
    `@shellx-motion/renderer-browser`. It is resolved from the npm registry at
    install time and is never copied into this repository, so it is not
    redistributed here and needs no notice entry. Consumers who redistribute an
    installed tree, a bundle, or an installer that embeds it must carry
    Apache-2.0's own notice requirements for that copy.
  - Chromium is located as an existing host executable at launch time; no
    browser binary ships in this repository.
  - FFmpeg and FFprobe are invoked as separate host processes. No FFmpeg binary
    ships in this repository, and any installation a user provides remains under
    its own license. See https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.
